# Collect Digital Engineering Standards

These rules apply to every task in this repository.

## Engineering Priorities

Always optimize for:

- Maintainability over shortcuts
- Small, reviewable pull requests
- Configuration over hardcoded values
- Strong typing and explicit contracts
- Reuse before duplication
- Long-term architecture over short-term speed
- Simplicity over cleverness

## Implementation Rules

- Extend existing architecture before creating new patterns.
- Keep business logic separate from presentation.
- Keep components focused on a single responsibility.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Explain architectural tradeoffs before introducing new patterns.
- Separate refactoring from feature development whenever practical.

## Data Integrity

- Never fabricate blockchain data.
- Never fabricate wallet data.
- Never fabricate marketplace metrics.
- Never fabricate social metrics.
- Never fabricate scoring data.
- Surface unknown data instead of guessing.

## Code Quality

- Use strict TypeScript.
- Avoid `any` unless unavoidable.
- Remove dead code.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Write deterministic, testable code.

## Product Mindset

When multiple implementations are possible:

- Prefer trust over engagement.
- Prefer explainability over hidden behavior.
- Prefer premium user experience over quick implementation.
- Protect long-term maintainability.